For my project, I used ChatGPT’s built-in image generation capabilities to create a picture of a sandwich. I chose this tool because it’s straightforward, accessible, and I’ve had positive experiences with its output quality in the past. My prompt was simple and direct: “Sandwich picture.” I wanted to see how well the model could interpret a basic, everyday concept without needing a lot of extra detail.
The image turned out exactly as I expected. It featured a classic sandwich with recognizable layers, bread, lettuce, tomato, and deli meat. The clarity and realism matched what I had in mind, which was important for making my project visually appealing and easy to understand. The generated image helped tie together my presentation by providing a clear, engaging visual that supported my written content, making the overall project more memorable and approachable for my audience.
